Given the following df:

df <- data.frame(lat = c(36.1, 36, 36, 36.1, 36.1, 36, 36), lng = c(-94.17, -94.2, -94.14, -94.2, -94.14, -94.14, -94.2), shape = c("triangle", "triangle", "triangle", "square", "square", "square", "square"))

> df
   lat    lng    shape
1 36.1 -94.17 triangle
2 36.0 -94.20 triangle
3 36.0 -94.14 triangle
4 36.1 -94.20   square
5 36.1 -94.14   square
6 36.0 -94.14   square
7 36.0 -94.20   square

suppose I want to overlay the df shapes onto a leaflet map via addPolygons().  Either of the following work well:

df %>% filter(shape == "triangle") %>% leaflet() %>% addPolygons(lat = ~lat, lng = ~lng)

df %>% filter(shape == "square") %>% leaflet() %>% addPolygons(lat = ~lat, lng = ~lng)

If, however, the order of that lat/lng arguments aren't just so (ensured by subsetting via filter() above), you get erratic plotting, eg:

