down votefavorite <http://stackoverflow.com/questions/34939600/using-postgresql-extension-quantile-function-with-dplyr#>

I have about 20 mil rows of data stored in my local postgreSQL database. I want to calculate 1,2,3 quantile of three columns, and I installed the quantile function from pgxn client,and the quantile function works fine within postgreSQL, as well as RPostgreSQL package.But I am trying to use the great dplyr with my postgreSQL database connection. below is my code
library(dplyr)
src <- src_postgres(db,port,user,host)
tbl <- tbl(src,mytbl)
summary <- tbl %>%
  group_by(group) %>%
  summarise_each(funs(quantile(.,0.25),quantile(.,0.5),quantile(0,0.75)),
                 one_of(c(col1,col2,col3)))

it gives me error message below -
Error in postgresqlExecStatement(conn, statement, ...) :
      RS-DBI driver: (could not Retrieve the result : ERROR:  function quantile(double precision, numeric) does not exist
    LINE 2: FROM (SELECT QUANTILE("fico", 0.25) AS "quantile(fico, 0.5)"
                         ^
    HINT:  No function matches the given name and argument types. You might need to add explicit type casts.
    )

Then I tried another way, this gives me the same error message.
sql <- select group,quantile(col1,0.25),quantile(col1,0.5) from db group_by group
tbl <- tbl(src,sql(sql))

So my question is 1.can dplyr work with postgresql quantile extension? 2. or is there a way to achieve what want to do without loading the data from PostgreSQL into R?

